on visit it displays all dynamic content default should be displaying loading until the ui is populated with the real data not static data, and let these pages their navlinks in their nav menu should be same as the manageruser.html code 
-on this page a particular card details is fetched and all it's indicated fields in the ui are display in their expected places and it has 3 buttons(Edit Card Details,Approve & Issue Card,Reject Application) if the Edit Card Details button link is clicked it leads to the cards-edit-user.html page, if the Approve & Issue Card is clicked it redircts back to same page and displays card approved and issued successfully.

-user recieves this notification below in it's dashboard notification modal
Title: Card Approved
Message: Your Physical Visa card(dynamic based of the type of card name) has been approved and is now active.
Time: 21 hours ago(dynamic based of the type of card name)
icon: bell icon 
link named view details leads to the  /user/notification.html page where all history are displayed 

and this message notifcation should also be pushed to user screen using this dynamic snipt of code according to the event that occurred

{/* For example, after a successful deposit, trade, withdrawal, or admin action, import the helper in that backend route:

const { sendPushToUser } = require('../utils/pushNotifications');

Then call it after the database operation succeeds:

try {
  await sendPushToUser(req.user, {
    title: 'Deposit confirmed',
    body: 'Your deposit has been successfully processed.',
    url: '/user/dashboard.html',
    tag: 'deposit-confirmed',
  });
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Push notification failed:', error.message);
} */}

